  "description": "<p>POSTing FOXML without a PID but with the pid included as part of the request gives an error that the PID is malformed</p>\n\n<p>Tried doing the following using Firefox Poster:</p>\n\n<p>POST to <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/fedora/objects/newpid:foo\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/fedora/objects/newpid:foo</a></p>\n\n<p>with FOXML as request data (note that no PID is defined):</p>\n\n<p>&lt;?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?&gt;<br/>\n&lt;foxml:digitalObject VERSION=\"1.1\" xmlns:foxml=\"info:fedora/fedora-system:def/foxml#\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"info:fedora/fedora-system:def/foxml# <a href=\"http://www.fedora.info/definitions/1/0/foxml1-1.xsd\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.fedora.info/definitions/1/0/foxml1-1.xsd</a>\"&gt;<br/>\n&lt;foxml:objectProperties&gt;<br/>\n&lt;foxml:property NAME=\"info:fedora/fedora-system:def/model#state\" VALUE=\"Active\"/&gt;<br/>\n&lt;foxml:property NAME=\"info:fedora/fedora-system:def/model#label\" VALUE=\"Label\"/&gt;<br/>\n&lt;/foxml:objectProperties&gt;<br/>\n&lt;/foxml:digitalObject&gt;</p>\n\n<p>Response:</p>\n\n<p>fedora.server.errors.GeneralException: Ingest failed: <br/>\n...<br/>\nCaused by: fedora.common.FaultException: Malformed PID: PID delimiter (<img class=\"emoticon\" src=\"/images/icons/emoticons/smile.png\" height=\"16\" width=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"/> is missing.<br/>\n\tat fedora.common.PID.getInstance(PID.java:77)<br/>\n\tat fedora.server.validation.ValidationUtility.validateReservedDatastreams(ValidationUtility.java:81)<br/>\n...</p>\n\n<p>What should happen in this case is that the PID provided as part of the REST request should be used as the object's PID upon ingest.</p>",
